WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.917
Begin with the mission objective and decision.

00:00:02.917 --> 00:00:06.538
Define the target, suspected condition, required detail, acceptable uncertainty,

00:00:06.538 --> 00:00:09.757
authorized area, and who will interpret the result.

00:00:09.757 --> 00:00:14.987
Avoid collecting a broad thermal survey when only one bounded question is legitimate.

00:00:14.987 --> 00:00:18.609
Select timing based on target behavior and environmental contrast.

00:00:18.609 --> 00:00:20.621
Building, roof, solar, mechanical, electrical,

00:00:20.621 --> 00:00:24.644
and search-support tasks may need different operating states and times.

00:00:24.644 --> 00:00:28.668
Coordinate with qualified personnel who understand the system being observed.

00:00:28.668 --> 00:00:30.277
Altitude, distance, angle, lens,

00:00:30.277 --> 00:00:34.703
and sensor resolution determine how many detector pixels cover the target.

00:00:34.703 --> 00:00:39.129
Keep within safe and lawful operating limits while collecting sufficient detail.

00:00:39.129 --> 00:00:42.348
An attractive overview may be inadequate for measurement.

00:00:42.348 --> 00:00:45.165
Plan coverage, flight speed, stable pauses, orientation,

00:00:45.165 --> 00:00:48.384
and overlap when mapping or comparison is required.

00:00:48.384 --> 00:00:51.200
Use repeatable routes and settings where practical.

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:56.029
Excessive speed or motion can blur patterns and reduce usable target detail.

00:00:56.029 --> 00:01:00.052
Complete aircraft, site, weather, battery, payload, storage, and calibration-context checks.

00:01:00.052 --> 00:01:04.478
Define abort criteria for wind, moisture, visibility, equipment warnings, poor contrast,

00:01:04.478 --> 00:01:07.295
privacy concerns, or an unavailable recovery area.

00:01:07.295 --> 00:01:09.709
Document the plan and protect privacy.

00:01:09.709 --> 00:01:14.135
Limit imagery to mission need, avoid unrelated people or private areas,

00:01:14.135 --> 00:01:16.952
and define access and retention before collection.

00:01:16.952 --> 00:01:21.780
Thermal capability does not reduce the need for lawful authority or proportionality.
